afk: a user interrupt no longer pauses an active goal.

Why: with interruptMode=wait a typed message queues as a steer, but the
TUI's empty-Enter queue flush (input-controller.ts setupEditorSubmitHandler)
and Esc both abort the active turn, and AgentSession.abort() defaults
goalReason to "interrupted" -- GoalRuntime.onTaskAborted then paused the
goal unconditionally. Every steer-by-double-Enter stranded the goal until
someone remembered /goal resume (observed 2026-08-11: goal paused at 15:08,
session ran interactively until 23:35 with the goal loop dead).

What must survive a rebase:
- onTaskAborted keeps ONLY the usage-accounting flush (with the
  reason=internal persistWallClock distinction); it never flips
  status/enabled and never persists goal_paused.
- Deliberate pauses stay: pauseGoal() (/goal pause) and onThreadResumed's
  auto-pause on session resume are untouched.
- Post-interrupt behavior needs no other change: the queued steer drains
  after the abort unwinds, and #scheduleGoalContinuation's guards (editor
  text, pending submission, 800ms idle timer) keep the goal from fighting
  a user who is typing.

